From aeaa25a8b869701937d4db5d4458477e9a6713fa Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 5 Jul 2026 23:22:56 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Fix non-functional install banner on iOS
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The install banner told every iOS user to "tap the Share button below,
then Add to Home Screen" — instructions that are wrong on iPad (Share is
top-right), impossible in non-Safari iOS browsers and in-app webviews
(no Add to Home Screen), and attached to a card that looks tappable but
did nothing, so users reported the install button as broken.

- Extract pure, unit-tested environment classification into
  src/lib/pwa/install-env.ts (iOS Safari vs non-Safari vs webview,
  iPhone vs iPad incl. iPadOS desktop-class UA, dismissal cool-down).
- iOS Safari: whole card now toggles numbered, device-correct
  install steps — no dead tap target.
- iOS non-Safari/webviews: honest "open in Safari" guidance with a
  Copy Link button instead of impossible instructions.
- Android/Chromium: unchanged real Install button via
  beforeinstallprompt.
- Dismissal now stores a timestamp with a 14-day cool-down instead of
  hiding forever (permanent only after actual install); the legacy "1"
  value intentionally reads as expired so everyone who dismissed the
  broken banner sees the fixed one once.
- Add explicit apple-touch-icon so A2HS uses the app icon, not a
  page screenshot.
- Add captureClientEvent() (gated, lazy PostHog) and instrument banner
  impressions, prompt outcomes, installs, and copy-link usage.

Verified via Playwright against the production build: 18 checks across
iPhone/iPad Safari, iOS Chrome, desktop Chromium (synthetic
beforeinstallprompt), standalone mode, and manifest/icon serving.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01M7YDVywyofrr6KBiAJqmqa
